data falsifier_self_host_wet_enrollment_note: String = "Nightly falsifier Wet batch enrollment authority (Wave 2 CI substrate, 2026-07-15): falsifier_self_host_wet_entries = template rows (always enrolled when green) PLUS frontier-flipped module rows ONLY when compiler_frontier_roster disposition is SelfEmitted AND a declared SelfHostWetReceiptBinding exists for that module_path. SeedRetained modules stay off the nightly roster — a not-yet-migrated module is a declared frontier row, never an enrolled-but-red wet receipt (all-green nightly = healthy; any red = real regression). Each binding row is added at the moment its module self-emits and its wet receipt is green locally; the frontier flip and binding are the enrollment gate."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_rehome_note: String = "2026-07-25 REHOME off affected-set falsifier (run attribution on #7199 / srv1-02): template wet receipts are build-verification (emit+cargo), not an affected-set control. Measured: namespace_import_closure ~21min and self_host_logic ~34min against a post-hoc 600s whole-receipt budget (July-15 basis) — wall spent before refuse. Cadence flag false unschedules gunbc_falsifier_batches green Wet batch only; roster retained. Kill-at-deadline LANDED 2026-07-25 (shell waits SIGKILL process group at the ceiling; completion-side backstop retained). Review #7199 OR for batch-2: either reactivate as expect_red with kill-at-deadline, OR park on a separate build-verification cadence with owner+date. Chosen arm: separate build-verification cadence (templates mix already-green ~100s receipts with over-budget ones — a single expect_red batch would unexpected-green the fast rows). See falsifier_self_host_wet_build_verification_cadence_note. SelfEmitted assemble-red receipts are the other arm's live consumer: falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries (Wet expect_red quarantine on the falsifier)."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_build_verification_cadence_note: String = "INTERIM home for green-wet TEMPLATE receipts (falsifier_self_host_wet_template_entries) after the 2026-07-25 rehome. Owner: #7199 falsifier lane (briansrls). Target date: 2026-08-08 — by then either (a) a dedicated build-verification workflow enrolls these rows under gunbc_falsifier_self_host_wet_receipt_wall_budget with kill-at-deadline on a sccache-healthy runner class, or (b) falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active flips true after a dated under-budget receipt on that runner class (typed AND). Until then: local recipe claim_batch --wet --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> --functions <csv>; falsifier green Wet batch stays unscheduled. Distinct from falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries (assemble-red SelfEmitted expect_red quarantine — live on the falsifier, not this cadence)."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active: Bool = false

fn falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_is_active() -> Bool {
  falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active
}

type SelfHostWetReceiptBinding {
  module_path: String
  entry: String
  function: String
}

fn self_host_wet_entry(entry: String, f: String) -> ScheduleWitnessEntry {
  ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: f, kind: ExecutionWitnessKind }
}

data falsifier_self_host_wet_emit_class_note: String = "The second template row is NOT a per-module self-host receipt — it is the emit-CLASS receipt for the Gate-1 import-closure derivation (emit_import_closure_root). It enrolls as a template row rather than a SelfHostWetReceiptBinding because it is bound to no single module_path: it proves a property of the EMITTER (an import-free namespace module referencing a sibling cross-module emits cargo-compiling Rust) on a synthetic fixture, so no frontier row flips to gate it. It is required coverage, not redundancy: regen only exercises the seed corpus, which is import-based, so the self-host fixed point is unchanged by the pass and cannot witness this class."

